A||||8||alpha1||Has anyone tried welding conduit?||||1||
Z||000000||alpha1||12-16-2000||04:28 PM||||Has anyone had good success with welding EMT grade electrical conduit? I have given it a quick try, but I did not clean off the clear coat and zinc at all and it did not weld very well. If I stripped to bare metal does it weld okay or is it just too low grade steel?||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||12-16-2000||04:47 PM||||Steel is steel. The only problem is the thickness (or should I say thin-ness). I guess it depends on how good of a welder YOU are.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||zeusrekning||12-16-2000||04:53 PM||||Don't know if it is like galvanized or not but the fumes emitted from welding galv. is very poisionouis(sp?)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||12-16-2000||06:16 PM||||It can be done- a friend made us a light duty welding cart out of it. He used a stick welder and did not burn it up, so a wire welder should be able to do it also.||||reg||1
Z||000004||alpha||12-16-2000||07:36 PM||||Okay, cool. I have a MIG welder, but I am not currently setup for gas....flux wire only. I think I can probably weld that thickness of material. I was a little unsure of whether it was steel or some cheap alloy.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fiero.dhs.org/fiero/sig.jpg">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu">douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||12-16-2000||08:26 PM||||Please, find something not galvanized or make sure you have a fan blowing it away from you. That stuff is really nasty when it burns off.<P>and yes, you have to clean away the galvanize before welding.<P>Basically you treat galvanize like lead. Zink is nasty stuff to get inside you. Wash your hands after working with it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||alpha||12-16-2000||08:55 PM||||Maybe I should just go back to my plan of using 1"x1" mild steel.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||12-16-2000||11:23 PM||||Yes- the mild steel is much easier to work with! Plus you won't have to worry about creating 3 armed offspring because of zinc poisoning  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Philphine||12-17-2000||05:13 AM||||i've done it but it didnt have to be really structurally strong for what i was making, 2" gauge pods. mig (i think, not a welder by trade just learned the basics as part of my job, wire with the non explosive gas) turned down pretty low.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||1
